Description: Wild OS Windows mode
 Runs a real copy of Windows in the background, and shows each Windows
 app as an ordinary window on the Wild OS desktop and in Start. Windows
 only runs while one of its apps is open; otherwise it is paused or saved
 to disk.
 .
 This package holds the system service that looks after Windows, the
 per-user agent that opens Windows apps, groups their windows and keeps
 their Start entries and file types, and wild-guest, the helper that runs
 inside Windows.

Package: wildos-winmode-runtime
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 libvirt-daemon-system,
 libvirt-clients,
 qemu-system-x86,
 qemu-utils,
 ovmf,
 swtpm,
 swtpm-tools,
 wildos-rdp,
 xorriso,
Description: Wild OS Windows mode, the virtual PC it runs on
 QEMU, libvirt and wildos-rdp, which Windows mode needs only once it is set
 up. Setting up Windows mode installs this package, so the Wild OS image
 and PCs that never use Windows mode do without it.

Package: wildos-run
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 python3,
 python3-gi,
 gir1.2-glib-2.0,
Recommends:
 osslsigncode,
 ca-certificates,
Description: Wild OS handler for Windows programs
 Decides where a Windows program or installer runs: as its Wild OS
 version, in Windows mode, or not at all with the reason why, using Wild
 OS's list of known Windows programs.
